  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For ideal gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>PM</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Graph between density versus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;should be straight line.</p><p>Graph between density versus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;should be straight line.</p><p>So graph between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> is not straight line.</p><p>Hence option II is wrong.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9ba5bb9c-b603-44a0-92ac-8283ce44a8a2-image.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 127px;\" /></p>",
